@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Bounded deterministic IFDS/IDE procedure-summary fixed point

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #495057
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F1F3F5
  BorderColor #495057
}

component "CodePropertyGraph\nfunctions and call sites" as CPG #DBE4FF
component "SummaryDomain\nfacts · transfer · summary" as DOMAIN #FFF3BF
component "call_graph_sccs\ncanonical SCC partition" as SCC #C3FAE8
component "IfdsCaps\nfive explicit bounds" as CAPS #FFE8CC
component "structural validation\ncurrent call graph · dense ids\nmembership · canonical DAG" as VALIDATE #F1F3F5
component "callee-first Kahn order\ncondensation sinks first" as ORDER #D3F9D8
component "acyclic singleton\nevaluate exactly once" as ACYCLIC #C3FAE8
component "recursive SCC\nbottom initialization\nbounded Kleene rounds" as RECURSIVE #E5DBFF
component "lattice contract check\njoin · subsumes · idempotence" as LATTICE #FCC2D7
component "IfdsOutput\nBTree summaries · seeds\ncaps · issues · iterations" as OUTPUT #FFF3BF
component "partial evidence\nno completeness claim" as PARTIAL #FFE3E3

CPG --> VALIDATE
SCC --> VALIDATE
CAPS --> VALIDATE
VALIDATE --> ORDER : exact current decomposition
ORDER --> ACYCLIC : non-recursive component
ORDER --> RECURSIVE : self or mutual recursion
DOMAIN --> ACYCLIC
DOMAIN --> RECURSIVE
CAPS --> ORDER
CAPS --> RECURSIVE
ACYCLIC --> LATTICE : candidate summary
RECURSIVE --> LATTICE : <latex>S_f^{(k+1)} = S_f^{(k)} \sqcup F_f(S^{(k)})</latex>
LATTICE --> OUTPUT : monotone update
OUTPUT --> RECURSIVE : current callee summaries
VALIDATE --> PARTIAL : malformed or stale
ORDER --> PARTIAL : work cap
RECURSIVE --> PARTIAL : iteration or work cap
PARTIAL --> OUTPUT : ordered evidence

note bottom of ORDER
  Condensation edges point caller to callee.
  Removing sinks first gives callees-first order.
  The smallest member NodeId breaks ties.
end note

note bottom of OUTPUT
  The CPG is read-only. No parallel graph is created.
  Capped output may omit may-analysis evidence;
  consumers must check is_complete() before a verdict.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF>| represented program |
|<#FFF3BF>| domain facts and ordered result |
|<#C3FAE8>| call graph and non-recursive flow |
|<#FFE8CC>| explicit resource policy |
|<#F1F3F5>| input validation |
|<#D3F9D8>| deterministic scheduling |
|<#E5DBFF>| recursive fixed point |
|<#FCC2D7>| lattice algebra boundary |
|<#FFE3E3>| incomplete-result evidence |
endlegend
@enduml
